From 961aeaaeb4088f284a81aa6734cdc79babac9984 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:18:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Add a USB HID keyboard next to MSC (-DHID_KEYBOARD=ON):
 picokbd's UDP 6869 commands

The netpipe Pico can now type into the X68000 Z itself, replacing the
separate picokbd Pico. x68key (PICOKBD=<this Pico>) sends the same
one-line commands (key / combo / hold / type) and gets "ok" back.

- Off by default; with HID_KEYBOARD=OFF the binary is byte-identical.
- MSC stays interface 0 (EP 0x01/0x81); the boot keyboard is interface 1
  (EP 0x82, 8 bytes, 10 ms). VID:PID stays 0xCafe:0x4002 so the Z sees the
  same MSC device; bcdDevice 0x0101 marks the HID build.
- hidkbd_cmd.c turns a command into HID reports one at a time (no USB or
  lwIP), with the same keys, 40 ms taps and persistent hold as picokbd;
  unknown key names now press nothing and reply "err key".
- hidkbd.c: the lwIP callback copies the line; the USB task's
  hidkbd_task() sends the next report when its time has come and the HID
  endpoint is free, never waiting (the same task serves the Z's SCSI).
  The 6869 socket opens once Wi-Fi is up, independent of netpipe, so a
  frozen Z can still be reset. Busy -> "err busy"; no HID poll for 1 s ->
  "err usb". MEMP_NUM_UDP_PCB 6 (DHCP, DNS, netpipe, hidkbd use the
  default 4).
- test/hidkbd: host test of the parser (make -C test/hidkbd).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PrGdt1XK1exBgERrMmLA1u
